From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:15:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] pcecd-bios

Before a disc starts slot checks BIOS/syscard3.pce, the System Card 3.0
the core boots (pce_fast_cdbios "System Card 3"): present, 262144 bytes,
crc32 0x6d9a73ef (the syscard3.pce row of libretro-database
dat/System.dat, md5 38179df8f4ac870017db21ebcbf53114). A 512-byte
copier header is skipped first, the same rule the core uses when it
loads the card (libretro.c HuCLoadCD), so a headered copy of the same
card reads as known. Missing or the wrong size: the disc stays on the
shelf with "PC Engine CD needs BIOS/syscard3.pce", because the core
refuses a disc without a card. Another 256 KB card launches with one
"syscard3.pce is not the known dump" toast a session. A disc resumed at
boot is checked the same way. The two toasts upload after the Disk
System ones.
